# ---- /admin/ must never appear in search results ----
# The <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow"> inside index.html only
# works if Google is allowed to crawl the page and read it. robots.txt used to
# carry `Disallow: /admin/`, which blocked exactly that — and, since robots.txt
# is a public file, also advertised the admin panel's existence to anyone who
# looked. The Disallow was removed; this header carries the same instruction at
# the HTTP level, so the page is crawlable, immediately seen as noindex, and no
# longer broadcast.
#
# The passphrase gate on this panel is a client-side speed bump, NOT
# authentication (see CLAUDE.md §9) — keep all three layers: this header, the
# meta tag, and not sharing the URL.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header set X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow, noarchive"
</IfModule>
